*
* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
*    members = !grp_members(group)
*
*    Returns the group's supplementary members, one per field, in the order
*    /etc/group holds them.  An empty answer means the group has none.
*
*    status()  0  read
*              1  no such group, or /etc/group could not be read
*
*    IT READS /etc/group DIRECTLY, exactly as !is_grp_member, !is_group and
*    !is_user do - the same openpath "/etc" and read.  No shell, no helper:
*    this is a question about a file SD can already read, and sd-elevate exists
*    for the writes, which are what need privilege.
*
*    THE PRIMARY-GROUP MEMBER IS NOT LISTED, AND THAT IS SAID RATHER THAN
*    HIDDEN.  A user whose PRIMARY group is this one does not appear in field 4
*    of /etc/group, so this cannot see them; answering that question needs a
*    /etc/passwd scan per user.  On this system nobody has an sdu_ or sdg_
*    group as their primary (measured 11 Sep 2026), and CREATE.ACCOUNT gives
*    every account a group of its own that is nobody's primary.  If that ever
*    changes, LIST.GRANTS would under-report, so the caller says where its
*    answer comes from.
*
*    dcount('') IS 1, NOT 0 - the correction GRANTA's do.list carries in the
*    port for the same reason.  An empty member field must count as no members,
*    not as one member whose name is empty.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
function grp_members(group)
$catalog !grp_members

   members.out = ''
   set.status 0

   if group = '' then
      set.status 1
      return members.out
   end

   grp.found = @false

   openpath "/etc" to gm.etc then
      read gm.rec from gm.etc, "group" then
         gm.lns = dcount(gm.rec, @fm)
         for gm.i = 1 to gm.lns
            if field(gm.rec<gm.i>, ':', 1) = group then
               grp.found = @true
               gm.members = field(gm.rec<gm.i>, ':', 4)
               if gm.members # '' then
                  gm.ct = dcount(gm.members, ',')
                  for gm.u = 1 to gm.ct
                     gm.one = trim(field(gm.members, ',', gm.u))
                     if gm.one # '' then members.out<-1> = gm.one
                  next gm.u
               end
               gm.i = gm.lns    ;* stop looking
            end
         next gm.i
      end else
         set.status 1           ;* cannot read /etc/group
      end
   end else
      set.status 1              ;* cannot open /etc
   end

   if not(grp.found) then set.status 1

   return members.out

* END-CODE
